{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "6f1c2a54-3b8e-4d57-9a41-5e2d7b9c0a11",
		"name": "MiniShop API - contract tests",
		"description": "Contract tests for the hypothetical MiniShop backend (QA take-home, Part B).\n\nEvery request has the contract payload saved as an Example, and a Tests script (pm.test) that checks status code, required fields, data types and business rules.\n\nHow to run (no live server exists):\n1. Local mock (recommended): in api-testing/mock-server/ run `npm install` then `npm test`. This starts a small mock that serves these saved examples and runs this collection with Newman.\n2. Postman mock server: Collection > ... > Mock collection, then set the baseUrl collection variable to the mock URL and use Run collection. The x-mock-response-name header on each request picks the matching example.\n\nRun order matters for the chained checks: GET /products, then POST 201 (saves orderId), then GET /orders/{orderId}.\n\nContract review notes for the API developer: see api-testing/api-contract-review.pdf.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"event": [
		{
			"listen": "test",
			"script": {
				"type": "text/javascript",
				"exec": [
					"// Runs after EVERY request in the collection.",
					"pm.test('[contract] Content-Type is application/json', function () {",
					"    pm.response.to.have.header('Content-Type');",
					"    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/json');",
					"});",
					"",
					"pm.test('[contract] Body is valid JSON', function () {",
					"    pm.response.to.be.json;",
					"});"
				]
			}
		}
	],
